John 2:13 | Alcuin, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): . Or Capernaum, we may interpret “a most beautiful village,” and so it signifies the world, to which the Word of the Father came down. | src: CAJohn.htm#2
John 2:13 | Bede, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): ; But He continued there only a few days, because he lived with men in this world only a short time. | src: CAJohn.htm#2
John 2:17 | Origen, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): ; Jerusalem, as our Savior Himself said, is the city of the great King, into which none of those who remain on earth ascend, or enter. Only the soul which has a certain natural loftiness, and clear in | src: CAJohn.htm#2
John 2:17 | Bede, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): ; Our Lord on coming to Jerusalem, immediately entered the temple to pray; giving us an example that, wheresoever we go, our first visit should be to the house of God to pray. And He found in the temp | src: CAJohn.htm#2
John 2:17 | Augustine, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): . Such sacrifices were prescribed to the people, in condescension to their carnal minds; to prevent them from turning aside to idols. They sacrificed sheep, and oxen, and doves. | src: CAJohn.htm#2
