John 2:17 | Bede, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): ; They then are the sellers of doves, who, after receiving the free grace of the Holy Spirit, do not dispense it freely, as they are commanded, but at a price: who confer the laying on of hands, by wh | src: CAJohn.htm#2
John 2:17 | Augustine, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): . By the oxen may be understood the Apostles and Prophets, who have dispensed to us the holy Scriptures. Those who by these very Scriptures deceive the people, from whom they seek honor, sell the oxen | src: CAJohn.htm#2
John 2:17 | Bede, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): ; Or, the sheep are works of purity and piety, and they sell the sheep, who do works of piety to gain the praise of men. They exchange money in the temple, who, in the Church, openly devote themselves | src: CAJohn.htm#2
