John 5:23 | Hilary, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): . All judgment is given to Him, because He quickens whom He will. Nor can the judgment be looked on as taken away from the Father, inasmuch as the cause of His not judging is, that the judgment of the | src: CAJohn.htm#5
John 5:23 | Chrysostom, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): . For, lest you should infer from hearing that the Author of His power was the Father, any difference of substance, or inequality of honor, He connects the honor of the Son with the honor of the Fathe | src: CAJohn.htm#5
John 5:23 | Augustine, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): . First indeed, the Son appeared as a servant, and the Father was honored as God. But the Son will be seen to be equal to the Father, that all men may honor the Son, even as they honor the Father. But | src: CAJohn.htm#5
John 5:23 | Augustine, Catena Aurea on John (Aquinas): . It is not, however, as being born of the Father, that the Son is said to be sent, but from His appearing in this world, as the Word made flesh; as He says, I went forth from the Father, and am come  | src: CAJohn.htm#5
